-- title:
--   Reading the compInf branch of the p-fibre as k(X₀(1))
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ with $5 \le p$ and a package $\mathfrak{X} : \mathrm{DRModelPackage}\ p$ of properness, flatness, integrality and normality data together with rational, geometric and fibral models for the two-chart integral model $\mathrm{DRModel}\ p$ built from the full modular function field of level $p$ and its $j$-invariant. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, with fraction field $K$ and a ring homomorphism $\iota_K : K \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and assume the pullback $X := \mathrm{DRModel}\ p \times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}} \operatorname{Spec} O$ is integral; let $\varphi$ be a ring homomorphism from the function field of $X$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,(1 \cdot p)$, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficient-embedded modular functions of level $p$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $k$ an algebraically closed perfect field of characteristic $p$, $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$, $\mathrm{data}$ a modular polynomial datum for $p$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence $h_{\mathrm{Kr}}$, and $h_\alpha, h_\beta$ the integrality of the two level-raising maps from level $1$ to level $p$; let $P$ be a place specialisation for these and $R$ a prolongation tuple for $P$. Assume $\iota_K$ carries $O$ into $A$ and that $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to k$ is the composite $a \mapsto \mathrm{red}(\iota_K(a))$. Write $\xi$ for the image of the generic point of $(\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{ratModel}\ k).C$ under $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compInf}\ k$ followed by $\mathrm{DRModel.baseChangeMap}\ \mathrm{to}\kappa$. Assume: $\varphi$ sends the germ at $\xi$ of (the image of) each $a \in O$ to $\iota_K(a)$ viewed in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,(1\cdot p)$; $\varphi$ carries every element of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,\xi}$ into $R.R_2.\mathrm{integers}$; elements of the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,\xi}$ have image with $R.\mathrm{residue}_2$ equal to $0$; and some element of $\mathcal{O}_{X,\xi}$ is carried by $\varphi$ to $\mathrm{jQFun}\ 1\ p$, the coefficient embedding of the $q$-expansion $j(q^p)$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a ring isomorphism $\theta : \mathrm{RatFunc}\ k \to \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ 1$, the subfield of $k$-Laurent series generated over $k$ by $\mathrm{jqModC}\ k$ and $\mathrm{jqNModC}\ k\ 1$, which is the identity on the constants $k$ and satisfies: for every $u \in \mathcal{O}_{X,\xi}$, applying $\theta$ to the image of $u$ under the stalk map at the generic point followed by $(\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{ratModel}\ k).\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$ yields $R.\mathrm{residue}_2$ of $\varphi(u)$.
--
--   This is the second-branch half of the identification of the two components of the geometric fibre at $p$ of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(p)$: the branch indexed by $\mathrm{compInf}$ has rational function field $k(t)$, and the statement pins down an isomorphism of that field with the level-one modular function field over $k$ compatible with $\varphi$ and with the second residue map of the prolongation tuple. It feeds the ordinal clause of [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.nodeResidue_eq_zero_iff_and_ord_eq_of_specializes_of_mem_maximalIdeal_swap`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.nodeResidue_eq_zero_iff_and_ord_eq_of_specializes_of_mem_maximalIdeal_swap), where the transported place is recognised as a Frobenius translate of a supersingular place.
